{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "description": "What a board running ESP-IDF's protocomm with security 2 does with each write, in order, on one connection: a script for a scripted board and a check for the real one. Each step is one write to an endpoint's characteristic (request) and what a read of it then returns (answer), or null when protocomm refused the write: protocomm_nimble.c then answers the write with ATT error 0x04 and keeps the characteristic's earlier answer, so a read after a refused write returns a stale answer and must not be made. event is the protocomm security event the board posted (credentialsMismatch is how a board counts wrong codes), boardLog the first error ESP-IDF logged, and setupHandlerRan whether the hsn-setup handler was called. srpCase names the board's salt and verifier in pairing-srp.json, and the code; a script with wrongPassword runs its first attempt with that password. boardDraws are the random values the board drew, in order: b (32 bytes) for each command 0 that reaches esp_srp (so not one refused for its length, its user name or its version), the session id (8 bytes) for each command 1 it accepts. clientPrivates are the phone's a, in order, for each command 0 made from one (A = 0 and A = N are made without).",
  "source": "ESP-IDF v6.1.1 (commit 051e4c4eb20346e043cdd47bc388fde75ff8af63): components/protocomm/src/security/security2.c, src/common/protocomm.c, src/crypto/srp6a/esp_srp.c and esp_srp_mpi.c, proto-c/*.pb-c.c; protobuf-c 1.4.1 (commit abc67a11c6db271bedbb9f58be85d6f4e2ea8389); Mbed TLS 4.1.1 with TF-PSA-Crypto (commit ce3f3485a121c100f58f36d700cb35b060f6e866). Compiled for the host and run by packages/protocol/src/pairing/esp-idf/make-vectors.sh",
